Rework status: decoupled client/server architecture
===================================================

The legacy map files remain unchanged for safe comparison while a new architecture is being introduced.

New apps
--------
- `/home/runner/work/watch-london-move/watch-london-move/backend` - TfL data aggregator and WebSocket streamer
- `/home/runner/work/watch-london-move/watch-london-move/frontend` - WebGL renderer (MapLibre + deck.gl scenegraph models)

Unified vehicle schema contract
-------------------------------
Backend payloads include:
- `schema`: `["id", "type", "line_name", "lat", "lon", "heading"]`
- `vehicles`: array of tuples matching that schema
- `details`: destination and route metadata per id

Backend features
----------------
- Continuous polling for configured bus and train lines
- Retry/backoff and simple cache windows to reduce duplicate TfL calls
- In-memory latest-state keyed by vehicle id
- Heading recalculation from movement trajectory
- `GET /health` for metrics (poll latency/errors/client count)
- `GET /snapshot` for debugging unified state
- Socket.io events:
  - `vehicles:full`
  - `vehicles:delta`

Frontend features
-----------------
- MapLibre canvas with deck.gl scenegraph layers
- `.gltf` low-poly placeholder models in `/frontend/public/models/`
- WebSocket subscription to backend stream
- Client-side interpolation between updates to avoid teleporting
- Rotation driven by heading
- Floating filter toggles for transport groups
- Vehicle click interaction showing destination + highlighted recent route trace

Phase-gated delivery alignment
------------------------------
- Phase 1: backend polling, normalization, health/snapshot endpoints
- Phase 2: frontend map canvas + streamed coordinate plotting
- Phase 3: `.gltf` vehicle models + heading orientation
- Phase 4: interpolation polish + filters + interaction

Local run
---------
1. Backend
   - `cd /home/runner/work/watch-london-move/watch-london-move/backend`
   - `cp .env.example .env`
   - set `TFL_APP_ID` and `TFL_APP_KEY` if available
   - `npm install`
   - `npm run dev`
2. Frontend
   - `cd /home/runner/work/watch-london-move/watch-london-move/frontend`
   - `cp .env.example .env`
   - `npm install`
   - `npm run dev`

Safe defaults
-------------
- Poll interval: 15s
- Emit interval: 10s
- Cache windows: 10s bus/train
- Retry: 3 attempts, exponential backoff from 1s
